  "articleBody": "Installing a basement door frame requires more attention than upstairs framing because basements feature concrete floors, foundation walls, and varying humidity. Selecting the right contractor ensures the door swings smoothly without binding against shifting subfloors.\n\nWhen evaluating a finish contractor for basement doors, look for someone who understands how framing interacts with concrete. A standard wooden jamb placed directly against a raw concrete floor can absorb moisture, leading to rot, swelling, and latch misalignment. Experienced professionals use decay-resistant or treated materials at the base and leave appropriate clearance to stop moisture transfer.\n\nQuestions to Ask Before You Decide:\n- Will the bottom sill or framing use pressure-treated lumber against concrete?\n- How do you verify rough opening dimensions across multiple height and width points?\n- Do you use low-expanding foam and shims at hinge locations to keep the jamb square?\n- Can you accommodate uneven slabs without trimming the door unevenly?\n\nA reliable contractor checks for plumb, level, and square on every plane before driving the final fasteners, ensuring quiet operation and even gaps around the perimeter.\n\nIf you are planning a basement remodel or need new door frames installed cleanly, contact Abraham Becerra at HH Remodeling LLC at 303-505-0866 to schedule a consultation.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
